From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Align raw sequences under Fil-C on AArch64

Long-distance matching stores 12-byte rawSeq values in an array and reads them
by value. The AArch64 ABI uses an 8-byte chunk for those copies, but the array's
12-byte stride leaves every other element only 4-byte aligned. Align rawSeq to
8 bytes under Fil-C on AArch64, padding each internal entry to 16 bytes without
changing its values or behavior.

--- a/lib/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h
+++ b/lib/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h
@@ -200,7 +200,11 @@ typedef struct {
     U32 offset;         /* Offset of sequence */
     U32 litLength;      /* Length of literals prior to match */
     U32 matchLength;    /* Raw length of match */
+#if defined(__FILC__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+} ZSTD_ALIGNED(8) rawSeq;
+#else
 } rawSeq;
+#endif
 
 typedef struct {
   rawSeq* seq;          /* The start of the sequences */
